{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790976696,"nonce":"EjM2Y+kfF3Uq5atzfmdruuxp6wQ=","message":"Landed on branch `worktree-agent-ac69fb8557d5f974b` (`52dfd66d`), design `doc/design/report.md` (`286cdf79`), over the plumbing of 09d9d09.\n\n`flows/report.star`, one function:\n\n    def report(from_=\"7d\", to=None, iteration=None, query=None)\n\nimported into the tracker and run against it. It resolves the window (an `iteration` id reads that issue's `start` and `end`, warning on `work.stderr` when either is missing; otherwise `from_`/`to` go down as the TIME strings they are), selects the issues, reads the two snapshots and the window's operations, and prints markdown. Returns `None`.\n\nCalls made:\n\n- The selection runs the jq program at BOTH ends of the window and takes the union, so an issue archived during the window is reported rather than silently dropped by the default `select(.fields.archived != true)`. The default is every unarchived issue.\n- Four reads, not 2N: `issue.list(\".\", at=from)` and `issue.list(\".\", at=to)` give the before/after fields and every parent's title; two runs of the query give membership; one `issue.log(\".\", from_=..., to=...)` gives every operation in the window, grouped by the entry's `issue` field. No per-issue call.\n- Created is \"absent at `from`\", which is exact because the replay makes an issue created later genuinely absent. Closed is the schema's status category (`completed`/`canceled`) becoming true, read per type and never from a status name. Archived is `archived` false becoming true.\n- Every changed field is listed `before -\u003e after`; the flow does not know which ones matter, and a missing line is worse than an extra one. `status` carries its whole path, `to-do -\u003e done (via in-progress)`, read from the operations rather than the two snapshots, because the states a task passed through are often the point of a week.\n- A value that is another issue's id is drawn as that issue (`8ade811 Bidirectional Jira sync`), and any other 64-character id is shortened: a report is read, not parsed.\n- Comments in the window are author, date and first paragraph cut at 200 characters.\n- Grouped by `parent`, the parent's title as the heading, title order, `(none)` last. Issues with nothing to say are skipped entirely.\n- `status` and `parent` are named in the flow, in the open: what to report is policy, Go has no field roles.\n\nQuickstart: a \"What changed since\" section (`--at`, the log window, `flow run report`, and that the output is markdown for a human to scan or an AI to summarize). The honesty test needed one fix: its walk read `report` in `flow run report` as a sub-command, so it now stops at a leaf command, which is true of `schema log KEY` and `flow export NAME` too.\n\nAGENTS.md: a \"What changed\" recipe row, and `report` named in the flows section after `board`.\n\nSample, two days of this tracker:\n\n    # What changed, 2d -\u003e now\n\n    18 created - 9 closed - 4 changed - 12 commented\n\n    ## Allocations: a matrix of work by time by people\n\n    - 0655187 Terminal renderer: the matrix view kind and the allocation type - created, closed\n      area: (none) -\u003e [tui, issue-model]\n      parent: (none) -\u003e 3289ec1 Allocations: a matrix of work by time by people\n      priority: (none) -\u003e high\n      status: (none) -\u003e done\n      type: (none) -\u003e task\n      comment - Luis Rayas, 2026-10-02: Landed on branch `worktree-agent-a9ffedc5230b1e31b`:\n\n    ## Weekly status report generated from the op log (workflow 2)\n\n    - 2c0c256 flow report: weekly status markdown from the op log - changed\n      status: canceled -\u003e in-progress\n      comment - Luis Rayas, 2026-10-02: Reopened and rescoped 2026-10-02: `report` is a flow in flows/ over the new plumbing (two snapshots and the log window), not a Go command. It resolves an iteration id or a duration to the window, sele...\n\n    ## (none)\n\n    - 2298f37 Board: a live kanban in the terminal and the GUI - changed\n      assignee: (none) -\u003e a3a2829\n      status: to-do -\u003e in-progress\n\n(The arrows are real arrows in the output; written out here.)\n\ngofmt, vet and the whole test suite pass.","files":null}]}